{#
_move_menu.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
"Move to" picker for the list toolbar and the thread view toolbar. Sits beside
_label_menu.html.twig and is the same panel on purpose — same button, same
surface, same indentation for nested labels — so the two read as a pair.

What it does not share is the interaction. The label menu is a set of ticks:
it stays open, and each click adds or removes one label. This is a choice of
ONE destination: no ticks, no confirm, the click applies the move and the panel
closes. So there is no `attached` state here and nothing to keep in step with
the selection.

No "Create new" row either, and not by oversight: a move needs somewhere that
exists, and the modal that creates a label comes back to a panel that has
closed. The label menu next door is where labels are made.

The entry for the list being looked at is hidden by the controller when the
panel opens, not here. The reading pane's copy is rendered by a request that
has no list behind it, so only the browser knows which view that is.

Variables:
  labels      Label[]   flat list of the user's custom labels (role null),
                        pre-ordered; indentation derives from label.depth
  targetId    int|null  the thread, in the reading pane; when null the pick is
                        handed to mail--list-toolbar, which owns the selection
  carried     int[]     ids of the labels the thread already has (reading pane
                        only); those are not offered, because a conversation
                        cannot be moved to where it already is. In the list the
                        controller reads the same thing off the ticked rows.
  placement   string    where the thread sits, from mail_placement() (reading
                        pane only): `trash` or `spam` takes that entry off the
                        picker. In the list, the view says the same thing.
#}
{% set LabelRole = enum('App\\Domain\\Enum\\Mail\\LabelRole') %}
{% set entry_class = 'w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-left
                      text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer' %}

<div data-controller="mail--move-menu"
     {% if targetId is defined and targetId is not null %}data-mail--move-menu-target-id-value="{{ targetId }}"{% endif %}
     data-mail--move-menu-carried-value="{{ carried|default([])|json_encode }}"
     data-mail--move-menu-placement-value="{{ placement|default('') }}"
     {# The bulk copy only announces what was picked. The toolbar it sits in
        knows the selection — including "everything in this view", which no
        row checkbox records — so the toolbar is what posts it. Left off the
        reading pane's copy, which has no toolbar above it to hear. #}
     {% if targetId is not defined or targetId is null %}data-action="mail--move-menu:picked->mail--list-toolbar#moveSelected"{% endif %}
     class="relative">

    <button type="button"
            data-action="click->mail--move-menu#toggle"
            aria-label="{{ 'toolbar.actions.move_to'|trans }}"
            title="{{ 'toolbar.actions.move_to'|trans }}"
            aria-haspopup="menu"
            class="group relative flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full
                   text-ink-muted
                   hover:text-ink
                   hover:bg-hover
                   transition-colors duration-100 cursor-pointer">
        {# Drawn here rather than taken from the icon set: a folder with an
           arrow into it is the sign Gmail taught everybody for this action,
           and Font Awesome keeps its version of it (folder-arrow-right) in
           Pro. The nearest free glyphs say something else — an open folder is
           "browse", an arrow into a bracket is "sign in". One path, the arrow
           cut out of the folder with evenodd, in currentColor so it follows
           the button's hover and every theme like the glyphs beside it.

           The viewBox is cropped to the folder itself. Font Awesome's glyphs
           fill their box edge to edge, so a folder drawn with the usual
           margin inside a 24-unit square came out visibly smaller than the
           tag next to it at the same nominal size. #}
        <svg class="w-[17px] h-[15px]" viewBox="3 4 18 16" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4.6l2 2H19a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v10a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2Zm9.5 3.5V12h-5v3h5v2.5l5-4Z"/>
        </svg>
    </button>

    <div data-mail--move-menu-target="panel"
         role="menu"
         aria-label="{{ 'toolbar.actions.move_to'|trans }}"
         class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 z-30 w-56 max-h-72 overflow-y-auto rounded-pane
                bg-pane-soft backdrop-blur-sm
                border border-line
                shadow-pop py-1">

        <p class="px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">
            {{ 'toolbar.actions.move_to'|trans }}
        </p>

        {# The three system places name a ROLE, not a label id. Their labels
           are made lazily — the first sync, the first delete — so a mailbox
           nobody has deleted from has no Trash label to point at, and the
           server resolves the role instead (MoveToService::systemTarget()).
           The id still rides along where there is one, because that is what
           the controller matches the Inbox row against to hide it. #}
        <button type="button" role="menuitem"
                data-action="click->mail--move-menu#move"
                data-move-role="inbox"
                data-label-id="{{ sidebarCounts.roleLabelId(LabelRole.Inbox) }}"
                class="{{ entry_class }}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-inbox w-3.5 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="truncate">{{ LabelRole.Inbox|role_name }}</span>
        </button>

        {% for label in labels %}
            <button type="button" role="menuitem"
                    data-action="click->mail--move-menu#move"
                    data-label-id="{{ label.id }}"
                    class="{{ entry_class }}"
                    style="padding-left: {{ 12 + label.depth * 14 }}px">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-tag w-3.5 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="truncate">{{ label|label_name }}</span>
            </button>
        {% endfor %}

        <div class="border-t border-line mt-1 pt-1">
            {% for role, icon in { spam: 'fa-circle-exclamation', trash: 'fa-trash' } %}
                <button type="button" role="menuitem"
                        data-action="click->mail--move-menu#move"
                        data-move-role="{{ role }}"
                        class="{{ entry_class }}">
                    <i class="fa-solid {{ icon }} w-3.5 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="truncate">{{ LabelRole.from(role)|role_name }}</span>
                </button>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
